  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full set at Middle East Downstairs in Cambridge, Massachusetts, on Tuesday, September 26, 2006 [1]. This concert is the 100th in the archive’s collection for the band, following a previous show on September 24, 2006, at the Pearl Street Clubroom [3]. The recording, titled tmg2006-09-26, was taped by Peter Sohriakoff and contains 18 songs with a total runtime of 76 minutes [1]. The setlist includes tracks such as “Wild Sage,” “In the Hidden Places,” “Color in Your Cheeks,” “Love Love Love,” “Dance Music,” “Old College Try,” “Baboon,” “Twin Human Highway Flares,” “Half Dead,” “The Monkey Song,” “New Monster Avenue,” “It Froze Me,” “Broom People,” “Song for Dennis Brown,” “This Year,” “Houseguest,” “No Children,” and “Going to Georgia” [1]. The song “Half Dead” is noted as rare, with only nine archived performances [3]. The upload description indicates the presence of two encores [1]. A listener review for this specific recording, posted on January 27, 2007, by MovingWater, suggests the show may actually be from September 26 rather than September 24 [2]. The recording has a rating of 3 out of 5 from one listener [1].",
